---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import portrait from '../../ashmit-profile.jpg';
import ProteinComparison from '../components/ProteinComparison.astro';
import PayoffTable from '../components/PayoffTable.astro';
import SalaryBars from '../components/SalaryBars.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="hero">
      <h1>I build ML systems and experiments, then check whether their results hold up.</h1>
      <p>Computer Science with a minor in Economics at NYU Abu Dhabi, expected May 2027. I research how AI advice changes the decisions people make together.</p>
    </header>

    <section id="research" aria-labelledby="work-heading">
      <h2 class="visually-hidden" id="work-heading">Selected work</h2>
      <div class="work-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>work</span><span>what I did</span><span>what the evidence shows</span></div>
      <article class="work-row">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/human-ai-collaboration/">Human–AI collaboration</a></h3><span class="kind">research / 2026–present</span></div>
        <p class="what">Built the experiment platform, with Ben Rosche and Hanan Salam.</p>
        <div class="evidence">in development; <b>no human-study results yet</b></div>
      </article>
      <article class="work-row">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/protein-language-models/">Bio-LoRA and protein-model evaluation</a></h3><span class="kind">research / co-first author, unpublished</span></div>
        <p class="what">Built the signal-peptide evaluation and ran three model sizes on HPC.</p>
        <div class="evidence"><ProteinComparison variant="strip" /><span class="evidence-note">BLOSUM62 feature injection vs vanilla LoRA at 650M, 3 seeds; full fine-tuning led at 150M and 3B</span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="work-row">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/synthetic-pilot-lab/">Synthetic Pilot Lab</a></h3><span class="kind">research / capstone, in development</span></div>
        <p class="what">Built paired game engines and an independent evaluator.</p>
        <div class="evidence"><PayoffTable /><span class="evidence-note">scripted synthetic benchmark; group totals hid the error</span></div>
      </article>
      <article class="work-row">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/roomwise/">RoomWise</a></h3><span class="kind">software / prototype, 2026</span></div>
        <p class="what">Co-developed an iPhone and desktop chair-fit checker with Aadil Chasmawala; geometry code, not the language model, decides the fit.</p>
        <div class="evidence">67 automated tests pass in public CI; <b>not yet measured in a real room</b></div>
      </article>
      <article class="work-row">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/fieldlens/">FieldLens</a></h3><span class="kind">research engineering / prototype, 2026</span></div>
        <p class="what">Built a local-model tool that links each answer to its source records.</p>
        <div class="evidence">some answers cited sources correctly and still missed what was asked; fictional records</div>
      </article>
      <article class="work-row" id="experience">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/zeek/">Marketing ML system, Zeek</a></h3><span class="kind">industry / ML engineering intern, 2025</span></div>
        <p class="what">Built discovery, ROI prediction, explainability, campaign and feedback-learning components in a four-person team.</p>
        <div class="evidence">synthetic data only; no real-customer results</div>
      </article>
      <article class="work-row">
        <div><h3><a href="/work/salary-regression/">Salary regression</a></h3><span class="kind">course project, Fall 2025</span></div>
        <p class="what">Repaired a leaky train/test split, then re-evaluated against baselines.</p>
        <div class="evidence"><SalaryBars /><span class="evidence-note">error on 92 held-out postings; replaces an earlier R² from the leaky split</span></div>
      </article>
      <p class="work-also" id="projects"><span>Also: <a href="/work/hinglish-ner/">Hinglish NER</a>, <a href="/work/camp/">CAMP</a></span><a href="/work/">All work</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="direction-heading">
      <h2 id="direction-heading">Research direction</h2>
      <p>I work in computational social science and human–AI interaction. I want to understand how AI advice changes cooperation: a group can follow an assistant’s plan without building a shared understanding of what each member can contribute. My next studies ask when that difference matters: while people use the assistant, after it is removed, and when they work with someone new.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="manuscript" aria-labelledby="manuscript-heading">
      <h2 id="manuscript-heading">Manuscript</h2>
      <p><cite>Bio-LoRA: Biological Priors as Inductive Bias for Low-Rank Adaptation.</cite><br />Co-first author. Unpublished manuscript, 2026.<br /><a href="/work/protein-language-models/#the-manuscript">About the manuscript and my contribution</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="home-section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <h2 id="about-heading">About</h2>
      <div class="about-copy" id="background">
        <Image class="portrait" src={portrait} alt="Ashmit Mukherjee" width={96} height={96} format="webp" loading="lazy" />
        <div>
          <p>I studied away at NYU Paris and NYU New York. On campus, I’ve facilitated workshops for first-year students and worked front of house at the Arts Center.</p>
          <p class="tools">Tools in the work above: Python, PyTorch, Hugging Face Transformers, XGBoost, SHAP, scikit-learn, FastAPI, Empirica, Slurm, pytest, Streamlit, Kotlin Multiplatform, SwiftUI, ARKit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
